    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="21.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 21.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="506–509" ed="#liebermann"/>E s’il ne l’ad, dunc numerad il sun heimelborch . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.i"/>, e ait les a jur e a terme, s’il les ad; e li enterceur le<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.a"/> mettrad en guage sei siste main; e li auter le mettrad en la main sun guarant u a sun heimelborch, le quel qu'il averad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="506–509" ed="#liebermann"/>E si il ne l’ad, dunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.33"/> nomerad soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.17"/> heimelborh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.36"/> e ses testimonies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.37"/>, e ait les a jur e a terme, s'il les ad u<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.a-2"/> s'il les pot aver; e li enterceur li<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.1"/> [m]etrad en guage sei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.2"/> siste main; e li altre le mettrad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.3"/> en la main soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.4"/> warant u a soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.4"/> he[im]elborch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.5"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.b"/> . . . . . . . .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="506–509" ed="#liebermann"/>Quod si non potest, hemoldborh et testes producat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.d"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="21.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="264" ed="#robertson"/>E s'il ne l'ad dunc numerad il sun heimelborch [e ses testimonies], e ait les a jur e a terme, s'il les ad, e li enterceur le mettrad en guage sei siste main, e li auter le mettrad en la main sun guarant u a sun heimelborch, le quel qu'il averad.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="506–509" ed="#liebermann"/>21, 1. Wenn er aber solchen nicht hat, dann soll<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.d"/> er seinen Gewährbürgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#missing"/> und seine [Kauf]zeugen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#missing"/> nennen und sie zum Gerichtstage und zur Frist stellen, wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de.3"/> er sie hat (oder: wenn er sie haben kann <hi rend="italic">I</hi>). Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de.4"/> der Anefänger verpflichte sich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.a"/> selbsechster Hand rechtsförmlich; und der andere [der Besitzer] soll das [Vieh] in die Hand seines Gewährsmannes oder seinem Gewährbürgen zuschieben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.b"/>, welchen von beiden er stellen mag.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">21, 1. But if he does not have such, then he shall name his vouching surety and his [purchase-]witnesses and produce them at the court day and at the term, if he has them (or: if he can have them <hi rend="italic">I</hi>). And the attacher shall bind himself in due legal form with himself as sixth hand; and the other [the possessor] shall pass the [cattle] into the hand of his warrantor or to his vouching surety, whichever of the two he may produce.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="265" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, he does not have one, he shall name his surety and his witnesses, and produce them at the appointed day and the appointed time, if he has them, and the claimant shall give a pledge with 5 compurgators, and the other shall give the livestock into the hands of his warrantor or his surety, whichever of these he has.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="507">ECf 38; ECf 39</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. Ed Cf. 38. 39</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 264–265 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 506–509, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> e ses testimonies <hi rend="italic">aus IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply e ses testimonies from IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dunt <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dunt Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heunel. <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> heuuel. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heunel. Im; heuuel. Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">testimoines <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> testemonies <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">testimoines Im; testemonies Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rest von</hi> 21, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt, obwohl</hi> 21, 3 <hi rend="italic">darauf Bezug nimmt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the rest of 21, 1 is missing, although 21, 3 refers to it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">anders unten</hi> 45 <hi rend="italic">f. aus anderer Quelle.</hi> Ed. Conf. 39, 2 <hi rend="italic">weiss schon von einer Einschränkung der Verpflichtung, nur unter Gewährbürgschaft zu kaufen, noch unter Wilhelm I. Schon vor</hi> 1066 <hi rend="italic">kennt die</hi> Denalagu <hi rend="italic">den Gewährbürgen als</hi> borh (I Atr. 3; III Atr. 5) <hi rend="italic">oder auch</hi> borhhand (<hi rend="italic">Urkunde Peterboroughs bei Birch</hi> Cart. Sax. 1130) <hi rend="italic">und</hi> festerman (<hi rend="italic">ebd. und Londoner Rubricator des</hi> Ed. Conf. 38, <hi rend="italic">um</hi> 1210)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">differently below</hi> 45 <hi rend="italic">f. from another source.</hi> Ed. Conf. 39, 2 <hi rend="italic">already knows of a restriction, still under William I, of the obligation to buy only with a warrantor. Even before</hi> 1066 <hi rend="italic">the</hi> Denalagu <hi rend="italic">knows the warrantor as</hi> borh (I Atr. 3; III Atr. 5) <hi rend="italic">or also</hi> borhhand (<hi rend="italic">Peterborough charter in Birch</hi> Cart. Sax. 1130) <hi rend="italic">and</hi> festerman (<hi rend="italic">ibid. and the London rubricator of</hi> Ed. Conf. 38, <hi rend="italic">c.</hi> 1210)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übersetzt aus</hi> hit sylle on wed</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">translated from hit sylle on wed</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.a-2" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u — aver <hi rend="italic">wohl Glosse</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u — aver probably a gloss</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">liueriad <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> luneral <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">liueriad Io; luneral Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">metirad <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">metirad Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">508</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heuuelborth <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> hennelborh <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heuuelborth Io; hennelborh Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">509</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zur Busse, falls sich der Anefang als unberechtigt erweisen sollte</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">as compensation, should the attachment prove unjustified</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">509</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. dagegen</hi> 21, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">see, on the other hand,</hi> 21, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de.1__2" n="1. 2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gewährbürge 1. 5; Kaufzeugen 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gewährbürge 1. 5; Kaufzeugen 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 21{5}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 21{5}</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. u</hi>. 21, 3{1}; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Anefang 5. b. 6. ‘<hi rend="italic">Se mettre en droit gage</hi> se dit lorsque quelq’un prouve, que son accusation est fondée (Laurière)’ La Curne s. v. <hi rend="italic">gage</hi> 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. below</hi> 21, 3{1}; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Anefang 5. b. 6. ‘<hi rend="italic">Se mettre en droit gage</hi> se dit lorsque quelq’un prouve, que son accusation est fondée (Laurière)’ La Curne s. v. <hi rend="italic">gage</hi> 16</seg></note>
